# Hual02 route (item59, re-authored by item67): player input from the vent spawn to Carrington's
# cell and the exit plateau, objectives driven only by the game's own chains.
#
# Player input (no set_goal/take_control): crouch-crawl through the ceiling vent
# (spawn 104,1840,-4536 -> gallery), two aimed shots break the two grates
# (BreakableMover5 at 104,1192 yaw 270; BreakAbleMover2 at -496,-688 yaw 259.5,
# measured legs 9-12), crawl the duct and drop into the office floor -4856,
# walk the underfloor to the service lift lobby (the corridor's Porte11 is opened
# by real input: the game's Grab tail -> Porte11.PlayerTrigger), ride the lift (item67:
# the game's own LiftButton0.PlayerTrigger -> LiftManager states -> LiftCage key move;
# the player is carried by the decoded mover-base attachment), then a labelled teleport
# for the sealed floor-2 lobby exit (the item67 next blocker) to the depot reader.
#
# Labelled diagnostic: the hostile BaseSoldier* pawns are removed by the test
# (remove_soldiers). Under the real level clock the unmodified level's underfloor
# gauntlet (BaseSoldier26 (-1714.7,894.9), BaseSoldier27 (-2218.2,698.9, shotgun +
# grenades), BaseSoldier25 (-1923.3,-1094.1), lobby BaseSoldier15/28, upper
# BaseSoldier14) kills the unarmoured player at t~130-138 near (-1834,773)..
# (-1663,1146) (measured; crouching does not save the player). That kill is the
# pinned next blocker for playing this level through.
#
# Labelled teleports, each for a measured movement gap (see the report):
# - "lift exit"      t=240 (-5200,872): the floor-2 lobby exit is sealed (the pinned
#                    item67 next blocker): the LiftManager opens its two LiftDoor outer
#                    leaves, but the doorway's third leaf Porte20 ('porte_haut',
#                    TriggerControl) is not in the manager's Floor2_OuterDoors set, never
#                    triggers and stays closed; the walker is pinned at its panel plane
#                    (y=2346, x=-2209) after the ride. The teleport lands at the depot
#                    reader (MagneticPassTrigger1 at -5259,803), which the route then uses
#                    by real input (t=242.5: aim-focus TargetActor=MagneticPassTrigger1,
#                    bCanTrigger=true, Grab runs; Porte19 stays KeyNum=0, asserted).
# - "depot"          t=244 (-8880,722): Porte19 is TriggerControl behind the magnetic-card
#                    chain and stays locked in this sim: the only card pickup
#                    (Hual02MagneticCardPick4 at -3474,1550) sits in the petitesalle whose
#                    walkable envelope is sealed from the corridor (measured probe: the walker
#                    is stopped at y=1698 outside and y=1595 inside, x -3461..-3420; the access
#                    runs through the meeting-room chain whose promotion is blocked upstream,
#                    item59's DV21 float and CWndSFXTrigger stall). The landing inside
#                    CineTrigger6 also starts the game's own Carrington scene
#                    ('Carring_ShaftEnter'). The corridor west of Porte19 is itself blocked at
#                    (-6198,842) in this sim (measured probe, local/re/item67/out/west.txt),
#                    so the teleport also crosses that gap.
# - "prison entry"   t=250 (-10368,2800): the prison compound perimeter is sealed
#                    in this sim (Porte151 Locked opens only from Carrington's
#                    escort moveseq); the landing touches DetectionVolume14 whose
#                    'didact6' event completes goal 2 through XIIIGoalTrigger1.
# - "prison grille escape" t=256 (-10176,2900): the DV14 landing sits inside the
#                    simplified collision of StaticMeshActor1024 'grille_prison';
#                    measured leg31: the player is pinned until moved.
# - "stair head"     t=304 (-14896,656,438): the exit stairwell pins the walker at
#                    (-14078,1314,35) (measured legs 20-23); the corridor beyond is
#                    sealed by the Locked Porte151, so the exit plateau is entered here.
#
# Weapon grant (labelled diagnostic): the player would carry the Beretta from
# Hual01b (the campaign loadout; Hual01a's route test documents no grant because
# the fresh-login inventory already has it). Starting on Hual02 directly hands the
# Fists only, so the route re-grants xiii.Beretta to make the two grate shots real.
#
# Objectives completed by the game's chains on this route (measured legs 31-37 and the
# fixture runs): goals 4/5/6 complete (the anti-goal completions), goal 3 promoted by the
# depot reader chain (MagneticPassTrigger1 -> Grab) but not completed. The promotion chain
# for goals 1 and 2 is blocked in this sim: DetectionVolume21 ('demarre_bureau', which
# promotes goal 1 through XIIIGoalTrigger3) floats 78 UU above the real duct floor
# (z=-4320, cylinder half-height 40, measured), and the eavesdrop scene's
# 'Blam' -> 'objectif92' promotion of goal 2 stalls at the unimplemented CWndSFXTrigger
# scene action. The DV14 -> 'didact6' -> XIIIGoalTrigger1 completion of goal 2 only
# validates a promoted goal (measured: leg37 with the diagnostic cue vs the fixture).
# (TouchTrigger8 z=63 gallery -> Cine7 'soldat_plan' raid -> 'soldat_assome' ->
# CineTrigger8 CineGoto -> Carrington moveseqs open Porte151 -> 'fin') is blocked:
# TouchTrigger8's gallery and Porte151 are both unreachable on foot in this sim, so
# goal 0 and the travel request stay unmet; the test asserts that measured blocker.
t=0.20 crouch 1
t=0.50 goto 104 1840 -4536
t=3.00 goto 104 1730 -4536
t=8.00 goto 104 1400 -4536
t=12.00 yaw 270
t=12.50 grant xiii.Beretta
t=14.00 fire
